# Authentication — API.md §Authentication, SECURITY.md §API access
#
# One bearer key, generated on first boot and printed to the log exactly once.
# Everything under /api/v1/ requires it; /health is the one exemption.
#
# The probes below use a path no endpoint owns. Auth runs as a layer around the
# whole router, so it answers before routing does: no key is 401 whether or not
# the path exists, and a good key falls through to 404. That is what makes this
# file testable without borrowing another file's endpoint.

@base = {{host}}
@probe = {{base}}/api/v1/auth-probe

### Valid key — expect 404, which means the key was accepted and routing ran.
GET {{probe}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### No header at all — expect 401 with code "unauthorized".
GET {{probe}}

### Wrong key — expect 401, and identically shaped to the request above. The
### response must not reveal whether the key exists or merely mismatched.
GET {{probe}}
Authorization: Bearer definitely-not-the-key

### Malformed header (no "Bearer " prefix) — expect 401, not 500.
GET {{probe}}
Authorization: {{apiKey}}

### Rotate the key. Returns the new key ONCE and invalidates the old one
### immediately — update `apiKey` in .vscode/settings.json before running
### anything else, or every later request 401s.
###
### Worth doing after a key has been pasted into a terminal, a chat log or a
### screenshot.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/config/apikey/rotate
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Confirm the OLD key is dead — run after a rotation, before updating the
### stored value. Expect 401, not 404.
GET {{probe}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### ─── Session authentication (dashboard) ───────────────────────────────
###
### The browser dashboard signs in with a password and rides a `__Host-`
### cookie; the bearer key above is unchanged and stays the scripting path.
### `login` is the only route exempt from authentication, and the only one
### refused when `[api] tls = false` (503 `unavailable`, no `Retry-After`).
###
### These are fixtures for the route-coverage gate as much as probes: nothing
### below is destructive except `logout-all` and `password`, and neither is
### issued by the test suite.

### Sign in. Expect 204 with `Set-Cookie: __Host-fah_session=…` and
### `Cache-Control: no-store`, and an empty body — the token is never in one.
### A wrong password is 401 `unauthorized` with no cookie; the two answers
### reveal nothing about which half was wrong.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"password": "the-dashboard-password"}

### Sign out this browser. Clears the cookie; the token itself stays valid
### until its absolute expiry — `logout-all` is the only real revocation.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Revoke EVERY session by rotating /data/session-secret. Every signed-in
### browser, including this one, is signed out immediately.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Change the dashboard password. Requires the current one (401 on
### mismatch, nothing written), enforces at least 12 characters (422), and
### invalidates every existing session on success (204).
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/password
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"current_password": "the-dashboard-password", "new_password": "a-longer-replacement"}
